      "bottomRightY": 246,
      "content": "Controls how the AcquisitionStop command and the acquisition stopped using a trigger (e.g. AcquisitionActive, FrameBurstActive, FrameActive or FrameEnd trigger), ends an ongoing frame. This feature is mainly used in Linescan devices where each line in a frame is acquired sequentially.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 253,
      "bottomRightX": 752,
      "bottomRightY": 287,
      "content": "- **Complete**: When stopped during a frame, the device will continue acquisition of lines until the specified Height is reached to deliver a complete default size frame.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 95,
      "topLeftY": 288,
      "bottomRightX": 697,
      "bottomRightY": 324,
      "content": "Note that if each line is triggered from an external source and this line trigger stops no frame is delivered, and an AcquisitionAbort is needed.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 74,
      "topLeftY": 325,
      "bottomRightX": 740,
      "bottomRightY": 358,
